  "configuration_id": "config_033",
  "reason": "Evidence: The best configuration so far is config_039 (scvi_n200 + imagenet_vit_l + transformer + weighted) at 0.725 acc, showing a clear multimodal gain over RNA-only scvi_n200 (0.653). However, image-only resnet50 performed very poorly (0.208), creating uncertainty about whether the ViT's strong pretrained visual features are essential for the multimodal gain or whether any image encoder contributes useful complementary information. Question tested: config_033 (scvi_n200 + resnet50 + transformer + weighted) is a direct ablation of config_039, differing only in the image encoder. This isolates the contribution of image encoder quality to the multimodal performance. Why best next experiment: It is the cleanest single-variable comparison against the current best, directly clarifying whether the ~7-point multimodal gain depends on ViT-specific features or is more general. This has high practical value (ViT is more expensive) and will inform whether to further optimize the image branch or invest elsewhere. The small weighted-vs-concat difference (0.725 vs 0.721) suggests fusion strategy is less critical than encoder choice, making this the higher-information experiment."
}

